{
  "schema": "semio.store.command-rejection/v1",
  "description": "Every producer of a refused command batch answers `CommandRejectionV1` (`🏪️store/🔄️sync/🧬️schema/🔣️command-rejection`). `hub` rows are the hub's `ApplyOutcome::Rejected` as it arrives: `reason` and the UTF-8 text of its `messages` bytes (the hub's `encode_messages` JSON, or anything else a wire may carry); `expect` is the one rejection both actors decode it into, exactly once. `local` rows are refusals an actor answers before any frame leaves it; `expect` is the rejection both actors emit. The Rust actor and the TypeScript actor must both produce every `expect` byte-for-byte in value (ticket 26/09/30 NON-DESTRUCTIVE-HISTORY-EDITING follow-up 3: a local counter `[69]` in the old `messages: bytes` slot reached the shell's JSON decode as the text `E` and threw out of the worker's message handler).",
  "hub": [
    {
      "name": "a graded concurrent edit",
      "reason": "command c-2 touches region(s) also touched by concurrent command c-1",
      "messages": "[{\"level\":\"warning\",\"code\":\"mutation.clamped\",\"message\":\"command c-2 touches region(s) also touched by concurrent command c-1\",\"target\":[\"features/f-1/properties/name\"]}]",
      "expect": {
        "kind": "rejected",
        "code": "hub.refused",
        "reason": "command c-2 touches region(s) also touched by concurrent command c-1",
        "messages": [
          {
            "level": "warning",
            "code": "mutation.clamped",
            "message": "command c-2 touches region(s) also touched by concurrent command c-1",
            "target": [
              "features/f-1/properties/name"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
